net/sched: sch_cake: make the cake_mq shared-shaper divisor track real concurrency

cake_mq installs one cake instance per TX queue, all sharing a single
config, so the aggregate rate cap rests entirely on the shared-shaper
divisor:

	new_rate = cfg->rate_bps / num_active_qs

num_active_qs is recomputed by whichever queue wins the sync tick, and
counted the queues that either had backlog or had *dequeued* within the
last tick (WRITE_ONCE(q->last_active, now) lives in cake_dequeue). The
activity window was therefore the sync tick itself, g_sync_time_ns =
200us, a value with no relation to the shaper timescale.

Measured on a GL-MT6000 (16 TX queues on the WAN, shared cap 900Mbit).
During an 802Mbit single-stream upload, with all 16 queues demonstrably
carrying traffic (per-queue packet deltas over the run ranged from 721
to 118802), tc showed the 16 children holding *five different* divisors
at the same instant -- 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 -- for several seconds, i.e.
per-child rates from 150Mbit to 900Mbit, summing to about 5.6Gbit
against a 900Mbit shared cap. Since each child re-reads the shared
value on every dequeue and reconfigures itself when it differs, a
spread that persists while every queue is busy means the shared value
itself is flapping between ticks and each child keeps whichever sample
it happened to draw.

Decouple the activity window from the tick. Backlog stays the primary
criterion; the window is only the short tail kept for a queue that has
just drained, so that a queue momentarily empty between two dequeue
bursts does not drop out of the count. A queue that has just *received*
a packet also counts as active, before its first dequeue, so the count
ramps up with a new flow.

The default window is deliberately short rather than large: on this box
idle traffic only touches a given queue a few times per second (measured
at 2-3 of the 16 queues active within any 50ms window at idle), so a 1ms
window keeps the spurious contribution near zero and a single-stream
upload reads num_active_qs = 1, i.e. the full 900Mbit. A window of the
order of 100ms would count that idle chatter and cap a lone flow to
roughly a third of the line.

The window is exposed through debugfs, like sync_time_ns, so it can be
retuned without reflashing.

--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -83,6 +83,17 @@
 #define CAKE_FLOW_MASK 63
 #define CAKE_FLOW_NAT_FLAG 64
 static u64 g_sync_time_ns = 200*NSEC_PER_USEC;
+/* Fenetre d'activite du shaper partage cake_mq. Le backlog
+ * (other_qlen) est le critere principal ; cette fenetre n'est que
+ * la queue gardee pour une file qui vient de se vider, afin qu'une
+ * file momentanement vide entre deux rafales ne sorte pas du
+ * compte. Dimensionnee sur le debit de paquets par file, pas sur la
+ * periode de tick : mesure a vide, la telescript du routeur ne
+ * touche chaque file que quelques fois par seconde, donc 1 ms garde
+ * la contribution parasite quasi nulle, la ou 100 ms compteraient
+ * ce bruit et plafonneraient un flux unique au tiers de la ligne.
+ */
+static u64 g_active_window_ns = 1*NSEC_PER_MSEC;
 static unsigned int cake_mq_queue_count(const struct net_device *dev)
 {
 	unsigned int ntx = READ_ONCE(dev->real_num_tx_queues);
@@ -1809,6 +1820,12 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Une file qui vient de recevoir un paquet est active pour le
+	 * diviseur du shaper partage, avant meme son premier dequeue :
+	 * le compte monte ainsi des l'arrivee d'un nouveau flux.
+	 */
+	WRITE_ONCE(q->last_active, now);
+
 	if (unlikely(len > b->max_skblen))
 		b->max_skblen = len;
 
@@ -2036,6 +2053,8 @@
 	if (cfg->is_shared && q->rate_ns) {
 		u64 last_checked = READ_ONCE(cfg->shared_last_checked);
 		u32 active_queues = READ_ONCE(cfg->shared_active_queues);
+		u64 now_ns = ktime_to_ns(now);
+		u64 active_since = now_ns - min(now_ns, g_active_window_ns);
 
 		if (now - last_checked >= g_sync_time_ns &&
 		    spin_trylock(&cfg->sync_lock)) {
@@ -2060,7 +2079,7 @@
 					other_qlen = READ_ONCE(other_sch->q.qlen);
 					other_last_active = READ_ONCE(other_priv->last_active);
 
-					if (other_qlen || other_last_active > last_checked)
+					if (other_qlen || other_last_active > active_since)
 						num_active_qs++;
 				}
 
@@ -3404,6 +3423,8 @@
 		struct dentry *cake_mq_debugfs = debugfs_create_dir("cake_mq", NULL);
 
 		debugfs_create_u64("sync_time_ns", 0644, cake_mq_debugfs, &g_sync_time_ns);
+		debugfs_create_u64("active_window_ns", 0644, cake_mq_debugfs,
+				   &g_active_window_ns);
 	}
 
 	return ret;
